        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "The new architecture retains BlockSparseMLP's conditional all-expert/fused-buffer cardinality mismatch.",
        "trigger": "Forward one flattened token through fully EXL3 expert projections with activate_all_experts=True and num_experts unequal to num_experts_per_tok; the reference configurations use 128 versus eight.",
        "expected_behavior": "Evaluate every expert for capture, or select an ordinary path that supports the all-expert count.",
        "actual_behavior": "topk returns 128 expert indices but fused gate/up buffers have eight expert slots. exl3_mgemm checks the index dimension against the output expert dimension and rejects this combination. TransformerBlock.forward directly forwards params to the MLP; ParallelDecoderBlock is another parent-tree forwarding site, but the new model uses TransformerBlock. Conversion supplies the flag, although inspected code does not establish that ordinary conversion also supplies the fully EXL3, single-token conditions.",
